# width: 120
# `ui.sidebar = .auto` (src/app/sidebar_auto.zig): the left column hides
# itself and slides back OVER the editor when the pointer rests in
# column 0. The proof that nothing was re-laid-out is the marker at
# column 95 of the open file: an editor squeezed beside a docked 30-cell
# tree clips it, an editor that kept its full width shows it. It is on
# screen while the overlay is up, and only disappears once the panel is
# PINNED — which is when a relayout is the point.
write .mnml/config.zon .{ .ui = .{ .sidebar = .auto, .sidebar_reveal_ms = 40, .sidebar_hide_ms = 40 } }
write wide.txt "...............................................................................................ENDMARK\n"
write zz_marker.txt "nothing opens this\n"
open wide.txt
# The overlay's signature is the pin chip 󰐃 in its header strip —
# a glyph nothing else on the screen paints, so it cannot be confused
# with a tooltip or a tab that happens to carry a section's name.
# Hidden: no panel, and the editor has the whole width.
expect screen lacks "󰐃"
expect screen lacks "zz_marker"
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
# The pointer rests in column 0: after the dwell the panel is up, over
# the editor — the tree's own file is on screen and the far marker
# still is, so no pane moved.
hover 0 10
wait 200
expect screen contains "󰐃"
expect screen contains "zz_marker"
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
# Resting on the panel itself keeps it up.
hover 12 10
wait 200
expect screen contains "zz_marker"
# The pointer leaves: `sidebar_hide_ms` later it is gone and the editor
# is uncovered.
hover 90 20
wait 300
expect screen lacks "zz_marker"
expect screen contains "ENDMARK"
